---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const intro = 'My journey has been shaped by a lifelong quest to understand why, amidst material abundance, so many of us remain spiritually starved.';
const paras = [
  'From a young age, I was curious about the role of the divine — or whether such a thing existed at all — and whether a wonderful life was truly possible. This curiosity led me to profound early experiences: the ecstasy of seeing the sun shine through the blinds in the morning, hearing the birds singing, and the overwhelming gratitude for the simple yet miraculous functions of my organs.',
  'However, my path was not without struggle. Years of disillusionment and depression made me realize that the contemporary spiritual beliefs I had inherited were deeply flawed. I saw myself living in a society of "rich slaves," floating on the surface but starting to sink. This realization led me to Colorado, where I sought more open minds and to study psychology and religion, with a focus on Taoist and Buddhist teachings.',
  'Feeling a deeper calling, I left the United States to pursue what I believed to be a humanitarian mission in Senegal with the U.S. Peace Corps. However, it was the people of Senegal who taught me more than I could ever give to them. They showed me that the essence of a life well-lived is not found in extraordinary comfort or extravagant experiences, but in a deep faith in the divine connection that binds us all — almost like family — to everyone we meet.',
  'After nearly two years in Senegal, I moved to Berlin to study neuroscience, earning a Master’s degree from Humboldt University in 2022. Yet, even after achieving this academic success, I felt an undeniable pull towards what I believed was part of my life’s calling: sitting with people and reminding each other to bask in our shared light of kindness, compassion, and understanding.',
  'Throughout my life, I faced fears, doubts, and pains, yet my yoga practice has always been my sanctuary — allowing me to transcend my flickering, often feeble mind. It was through yoga that I eventually found myself in the role of a teacher, a role that breathed life into my being and gave me a profound sense of purpose.',
  'My passion for yoga began at 18 and has since become the cornerstone of my life, guiding me with joy and inspiring determination. Inspired by my teachers, I developed a deep belief in the transformative power of asana and meditation, emphasizing the cultivation of compassion and intuition through embodied practice.',
  'Having had the privilege of studying with the founders of Jivamukti Yoga, Sharon Gannon and David Life, and completing my apprenticeship under Anja Kühnel, I was certified as an advanced teacher in 2021. I relish the opportunity to share this integrative and powerful form of yoga with you, within a vibrant and supportive community.',
  'In addition to teaching, I am the founder of the Jango Project, a nonprofit organization dedicated to enhancing the well-being and prosperity of children through initiatives focused on nutrition, education, and the environment. Driven by a desire to create meaningful change and promote holistic wellness, I do my best to fuse contemporary scientific knowledge with traditional spiritual wisdom to foster collective peace and alleviate suffering — both on and off the mat.',
];
---
<Base title="About" description="Conor Byrnes — yoga teacher, neuroscientist, and founder of the Jango Project." headerTheme="dark">
  <section class="about sec-yellow">
    <div class="container about-grid">
      <div class="about-text">
        <h1>About me</h1>
        <p class="intro">{intro}</p>
        {paras.map((p) => <p class="reveal">{p}</p>)}
        <div class="about-cta">
          <a href="/events" class="btn btn-green">Practice with me</a>
          <a href="/jango-project" class="btn btn-dark">The Jango Project</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="about-photo">
        <img src="/media/dsc01432-copy.jpeg" alt="Conor Byrnes practicing yoga" loading="eager" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .about { padding-top: 8rem; }
  .about-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.05fr 0.95fr; gap: 3.5rem; align-items: start; }
  .about-text { max-width: 60ch; }
  .about-text h1 { margin-bottom: 0.5em; }
  .about-text .intro { font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2.4vw, 1.6rem); font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.4; margin-bottom: 1.5em; }
  .about-text p { color: #1c1c18; }
  .about-text .reveal { font-size: 0.98rem; }
  .about-photo { position: sticky; top: 6rem; }
  .about-photo img { width: 100%; border-radius: 4px; filter: grayscale(1) contrast(1.03); aspect-ratio: 3/4; object-fit: cover; }
  .about-cta { display: flex; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 2rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .btn-dark { background: var(--ink); color: #fff; }
  .btn-dark:hover { background: #000; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .about-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2rem; }
    .about-photo { position: static; order: -1; max-width: 360px; }
  }
</style>
